54,3,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"I cannot support A, as it puts an impossible burden on the already depleted late-turn pool. B and C require roadway and structural work that our understaffed crews cannot sustain. D is the only operationally lean choice.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"D is the best fit. A and B don't solve the connection wait times I found, and C is just fixing the ""loudest"" parts of the station. D streamlines the whole trip.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate D is the only logical choice. It elegantly bypasses the paving costs and staffing shortages that make B and C liabilities, and it avoids the financial absurdity of paying three separate ticketing contractors.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Servas,,Candidate D is a most promising path. It honors the success of our previous contactless trials and avoids the physical struggles of the pre-war shells and depleted crews. It is a bridge to a more seamless future.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. Candidate D avoids the risks of the pre-war shells and the friction of inter-operator disagreements. It is the most stable and serene option, ensuring we do not encounter the hidden delays that plague physical works.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Asuka,,It is rare to see such immediate alignment. Candidate D is the only proposal that does not assume the existence of a workforce we simply do not have. It is the most responsible choice.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"I'm not interested in the other options. A and B are just more of the same, and C is a waste of effort. D actually addresses the system as a whole, which is what we need.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. It is quite refreshing when the path of least resistance also happens to be the most fiscally sound. Candidate D transforms a fragmented expense into a streamlined asset without requiring a single shovel of asphalt.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Servas,,"It is a beautiful thing when wisdom and practicality meet. By choosing the path that respects our current limitations and builds upon our past successes, we act with true stewardship for the city.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"It is a relief to find a solution that does not invite chaos. By avoiding the physical uncertainties of the old stations and the complexities of roadway work, we preserve our peace and the city's stability.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I am satisfied with the consensus. Candidate D is the only option that respects the reality of our staffing crisis and avoids the risks associated with physical infrastructure. I vote for D.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I'm voting for D. It's the only plan that actually makes sense for the whole journey instead of just patching up a few loud complaints. It's the most efficient way to fix the system.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall cast my vote for Candidate D. It is the only option that replaces our current financial whimsy with a rational structure, all while avoiding the logistical nightmares of our depleted crews.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I shall also cast my vote for Candidate D. It is a choice that honors the lessons of the past and provides a gentle, sustainable path forward for all. I vote for D.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I concur. Candidate D is the only choice that avoids the hidden dangers of the pre-war shells and the friction of operator disputes. It is the most peaceful path to success. I vote for D.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
